                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7f2f6013-7e90-4e37-9e6e-fcfe180425e3",
                        "source_entry_id": "a61bf6b5-6dce-3f5e-94cc-6933de227ff8",
                        "source_sense_description": "Pièce de machine à tisser",
                        "target_lang_word": "forebeam",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "forebeam",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "84936e9e-33f3-3061-8545-66ceb21b40ee",
                                        "entry_id": "22cd4521-4dbc-3c15-9a61-a2c4e5a2b555",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The breast beam of a loom."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44af5fd8-d9e7-4ece-9b59-8c7d221fdaca",
                                                "sense_id": "84936e9e-33f3-3061-8545-66ceb21b40ee",
                                                "text": "They are sustained at bottom with other strong pieces of wood in the manner of trestles; and, to keep them the firmer, they are likewise fastened to the floor with a kind of buttresses, which prevent any shaking, though there are sometimes four or five workmen leaning on the forebeam at once."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eac0740b-4eca-4e76-83d7-7df430e4976c",
                                                "sense_id": "84936e9e-33f3-3061-8545-66ceb21b40ee",
                                                "text": "{Just like the cloth that goes} from this side {of the loom, from the yarn-beam}, to that side over there {to the forebeam}, winding on there, and winding off here."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e8459f4-1415-43fa-b143-640f8739b5b4",
                                                "sense_id": "84936e9e-33f3-3061-8545-66ceb21b40ee",
                                                "text": "On the tenth year Frya's sister took the forebeam from the loom, put the rolling-pin crosswise and wrapped it with a baby bundle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5f06a4c5-7c86-314f-b0fb-da2a1c9f01e0",
                                        "entry_id": "22cd4521-4dbc-3c15-9a61-a2c4e5a2b555",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A horizontal spar across the bow of some sailing vessels, used to stabilize the hulls of a catamaran, to secure a bowsprit, or to tie down the tack when there is no bowsprit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a7f42b0-4278-45fe-9dd5-f6977ba47a8b",
                                                "sense_id": "5f06a4c5-7c86-314f-b0fb-da2a1c9f01e0",
                                                "text": "And herein also her forebeam to which her bowsprit was fastened, cracked clean insunder; and some of her timbers likeways in the hold we found defective."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95033394-c925-46d6-b402-bf5a90d739a2",
                                                "sense_id": "5f06a4c5-7c86-314f-b0fb-da2a1c9f01e0",
                                                "text": "Schooner Ketcham returned to Chicago with foretopmast gone and forebeam sprung."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63212e63-ec4d-4af8-b9e3-f7cca8c3957b",
                                                "sense_id": "5f06a4c5-7c86-314f-b0fb-da2a1c9f01e0",
                                                "text": "Turns of shock cord, securing tack to centre of forebeam, stretch as the wind increases. This allows the jib to move up, frees the halyard slightly so the tack and peak move away from forestay."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b345d3db-40f5-4322-a078-761ad7389fab",
                                                "sense_id": "5f06a4c5-7c86-314f-b0fb-da2a1c9f01e0",
                                                "text": "The advanced design of new cats makes pitchpoling less likely. The treacherous forebeam is gone, and the new hulls have been engineered stronger to resist twisting under stress."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee323cde-c5a3-43c0-b3b6-3d4b43873d13",
                                                "sense_id": "5f06a4c5-7c86-314f-b0fb-da2a1c9f01e0",
                                                "text": "If using an all-chain system, then also utilise rope with the stretch in the bridle arms and have a 'lazy loop' of chain to act as a catenary between the bridle attachment and the forebeam. The minimum length of anchor line should be five times the height from the forebeam to the bottom at high tide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "413ea3de-77bb-3aa3-814e-b8f4d6f156a8",
                                        "entry_id": "22cd4521-4dbc-3c15-9a61-a2c4e5a2b555",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The support section of a robot arm that goes from the main body of the robot to the gripper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17a97edd-f538-48d1-accd-4070cf6ce0d6",
                                                "sense_id": "413ea3de-77bb-3aa3-814e-b8f4d6f156a8",
                                                "text": "The joints in the kinematic chain of a robot between the forebeam and end-effector are referred to as the wrist."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61529961-5172-3063-ab57-9909d93fd710",
                                        "entry_id": "22cd4521-4dbc-3c15-9a61-a2c4e5a2b555",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The leading portion of a remote signal from a moving source."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0f57660-bbdb-4482-87c5-83b929986c40",
                                                "sense_id": "61529961-5172-3063-ab57-9909d93fd710",
                                                "text": "The upwind forebeam data, for F9L1R19 (flight 9, line 1 and run 19), F2L1R1 and F3L1R1, the corresponding surface wind velocities are 6 knots, 22.5 knots, and 33 knots respectively, were processed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1682575-3314-4add-a7d0-7bd44c9e21d6",
                                                "sense_id": "61529961-5172-3063-ab57-9909d93fd710",
                                                "text": "The signal is delivered and analysed by three sideways looking antennae; one pointing normal to the satellite flight path (midbeam antenna) and the two others pointing 45° forward (forebeam antenna) and 45° backward (aftbeam antenna) respectively (Francis et al, 1991)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9249983-5516-4e9b-a325-f0687cd70d72",
                                                "sense_id": "61529961-5172-3063-ab57-9909d93fd710",
                                                "text": "The monthly averaged backscattering coefficient for forebeam over Indian sub-continent for the year 1998 have been carried out."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
